---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const title = 'About Us | JSON Diff Checker';
const description =
  'Learn about JSON Diff Checker — a free, privacy-first JSON comparison tool that runs entirely in your browser with no uploads, sign-up, or tracking.';
---

<PageLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  eyebrow="About us"
  heading="About JSON Diff Checker"
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    JSON Diff Checker is an independent, free-to-use web tool built for developers, QA engineers, and
    anyone who needs to quickly compare two pieces of JSON. We built it because most "online JSON diff"
    tools either upload your data to a server, bury the comparison behind ads and sign-up walls, or
    struggle with large, deeply nested documents.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>
    Our tool lets you paste, upload, or load JSON from a URL and instantly see a structured, color-coded
    diff of what was added, removed, or changed — down to the exact key or array element. Comparisons are
    semantic rather than textual, so differences in key order or formatting never produce false positives.
    You can export results as a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) file or a Markdown changelog for pull requests and
    documentation.
  </p>

  <h2>Our approach to privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Every comparison happens entirely client-side, in your browser. We do not operate a backend that
    receives the JSON you paste, and we do not use tracking scripts or ad tags. You can verify this
    yourself by opening your browser's developer tools, going to the Network tab, and watching for
    requests while you use the tool.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Have feedback, found a bug, or want to suggest a feature? Visit our <a href="/contact-us">Contact Us</a> page
    to get in touch.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
